<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">João Maria Ferreira do Amaral</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1803–1849</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">João Maria Ferreira do Amaral was a Portuguese naval officer and governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/macau">Macau</a> from 1846 to 1849. He imposed taxes on the Chinese population, expelled the Chinese customs officials and stopped paying ground rent to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, turning Macau into a fully Portuguese colony. He was assassinated near the border gate in August 1849; China formally recognised Portuguese rule in the treaty of 1887.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/joao-maria-ferreira-do-amaral.jpg" alt="João Maria Ferreira do Amaral" width="320" height="389" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Not identified · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Joao_Maria_Ferreira_do_Amaral.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
